COMMIT bf299330145cd1a34da41552f3053554b8b31205
test(core): FIX-121 the TrailTest warning counts stop reading the whole JVM

Two counts in TrailTest totalled every Trail WARNING in the JVM rather than
the ones their own case produced — the same leakage FIX-54 fixed two sites
earlier. :648 now filters by the case's own `bad.key().toString()`. :630 could
not: its step 4 is the metadata-only row, whose warning carries no BlobKey at
all, so a key-only filter finds three of the four rows. Its second clause is
the delimited row head "message m-nw of flow f: " — never a bare id substring,
which is the trap FIX-54 hit, where "m-w" is a prefix of the "m-wait" fixture.

The counts 4 and 1 are unchanged and were re-derived from the fixtures during
review rather than taken on trust.

Checks: VERIFIED_PASS exit 0, TrailTest 13/0 (agent/work/FIX-121-green.log);
mutant Trail.java:164 key -> "K" EXECUTED_FAIL 13/2, killing the :648 count
(FIX-121-mutA.log); production byte-identical afterwards (cmp, git diff empty).
Disclosed: a mutant on the persist sentence at Trail.java:177 left all 13 green
(FIX-121-mutB.log) — that wording is unasserted anywhere, now row FIX-123.

